(3458516, 479679, 65547, '<td valign="top">Wow, my first ribbon!!!! I''m very very exciting, thanks for all nice comments, faves and votes! I really appreciate it!<br/> <br/>As I said above, this image was taken trough telescope Orion Optics Europa f/4.5 and 900mm of focal length. I was outisde capturing the eclipse for 4 hours and made more than 80 shots.<br/> <br/>Image was processed and converted to .jpg in RawShooter and then some touches in Photoshop CS2 - mostly levels and hue to get this red, in original moon was more orange.<br/> <br/>Thanks again, I really haven''t expected it!<br/> <br/>More my pictures on this link: //freeweb.siol.net/tcigler/nova/moon.html</td>', 'Wow, my first ribbon!!!! I''m very very exciting, thanks for all nice comments, faves and votes! I really appreciate it! As I said above, this image was taken trough telescope Orion Optics Europa f/4.5 and 900mm of focal length. I was outisde capturing the eclipse for 4 hours and made more than 80 shots. Image was processed and converted to .jpg in RawShooter and then some touches in Photoshop CS2 - mostly levels and hue to get this red, in original moon was more orange. Thanks again, I really haven''t expected it! More my pictures on this link: //freeweb.siol.net/tcigler/nova/moon.html', '2007-03-14 02:49:26.000000', NULL, 0),
