(3459081, 480226, 57886, '<td valign="top">Flott mynd Sigrún, hihi,  datt ekki í hug þetta væri þín mynd.... Glæsilegt og áfram Ice &amp; US :o)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-03-14 07:14:47.</i></td>', 'Flott mynd Sigrún, hihi,  datt ekki í hug þetta væri þín mynd.... Glæsilegt og áfram Ice & US :o)', '2007-03-14 07:13:12.000000', '2007-03-14 07:14:47.000000', 0),
(3459093, 478530, 43073, '<td valign="top">Hi Elaine, I was looking through your profile when I saw you had entered the red II challenge, so I popped over to see this entry and noticed there was only one comment on it. I hate that (when I enter and get few comments). I voted this challenge, so here are my thoughts on your shot: I gave this a 6.0. It''s nicely lit and the use of DoF really adds to it (I started it at a 5 and bumped it up during my review). The red is a really nice choice, too (not a comment I would outside of a challenge focused on color), and the lines in the thread give some movement (top to bottom) to the image (at least to my eyes). The one problem you ran into here with me as a voter is that string is just not very interesting to me as a subject. Some people don''t like kids, others don''t like cats. Me, I don''t like thread. Nothing you can do about that, but the technique shown on this with subject matter that interested me would have scored at least a 7, and probably higher.</td>', 'Hi Elaine, I was looking through your profile when I saw you had entered the red II challenge, so I popped over to see this entry and noticed there was only one comment on it. I hate that (when I enter and get few comments). I voted this challenge, so here are my thoughts on your shot: I gave this a 6.0. It''s nicely lit and the use of DoF really adds to it (I started it at a 5 and bumped it up during my review). The red is a really nice choice, too (not a comment I would outside of a challenge focused on color), and the lines in the thread give some movement (top to bottom) to the image (at least to my eyes). The one problem you ran into here with me as a voter is that string is just not very interesting to me as a subject. Some people don''t like kids, others don''t like cats. Me, I don''t like thread. Nothing you can do about that, but the technique shown on this with subject matter that interested me would have scored at least a 7, and probably higher.', '2007-03-14 07:19:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3459132, 479559, 33468, '<td valign="top">thankyou very much everybody for your comments :o)<br/> <br/>this shot was taken from a public viewing point, on the fence at turn one of the phillip island circuit in australia.<br/> <br/>i appreciate the shadows are a little dark, but the idea was to accentuate the red in the shot.<br/> <br/>i took this hand held (i dont own a monopod... or a tripod for that matter!), and i used a standard 55 - 200mm G lens.<br/> <br/>thanks for all your comments during the challenge, i would have been happy with top twenty, but this exceeded my expectations. i rated a little over thirty other images higher than what my average was, so i am absolutely stoked!<br/> <br/>cheers! ads :o)</td>', 'thankyou very much everybody for your comments :o) this shot was taken from a public viewing point, on the fence at turn one of the phillip island circuit in australia. i appreciate the shadows are a little dark, but the idea was to accentuate the red in the shot. i took this hand held (i dont own a monopod... or a tripod for that matter!), and i used a standard 55 - 200mm G lens. thanks for all your comments during the challenge, i would have been happy with top twenty, but this exceeded my expectations. i rated a little over thirty other images higher than what my average was, so i am absolutely stoked! cheers! ads :o)', '2007-03-14 07:30:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3459144, 478202, 67671, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, I was one of the 50 6s, I was put of by the washed out sky, or I would have scored higher, of corse it could be my monitor, but some of the tv eariels, blend into the sky, other wise excelent, very well done.</td>', 'Congratulations, I was one of the 50 6s, I was put of by the washed out sky, or I would have scored higher, of corse it could be my monitor, but some of the tv eariels, blend into the sky, other wise excelent, very well done.', '2007-03-14 07:33:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3459148, 479325, 23484, '<td valign="top">Once again, supurb detail and great color. Nice DOF and Great score.</td>', 'Once again, supurb detail and great color. Nice DOF and Great score.', '2007-03-14 07:33:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3459153, 479116, 23484, '<td valign="top">This is really a neat abstract shot. One of thos things you just can''t explain but is really neat looking.</td>', 'This is really a neat abstract shot. One of thos things you just can''t explain but is really neat looking.', '2007-03-14 07:35:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3459158, 477391, 23484, '<td valign="top">Relly cool shot Jayson. I love the angle. Once again you have the soft focus in front and the sharp focus in back. I don''t know if that really affects scores but it should have been higher than it was.</td>', 'Relly cool shot Jayson. I love the angle. Once again you have the soft focus in front and the sharp focus in back. I don''t know if that really affects scores but it should have been higher than it was.', '2007-03-14 07:37:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3459207, 478202, 33468, '<td valign="top">congratulations on the blue ribbon!<br/> <br/>a first class entry indeed :o)<br/> <br/>all the best, ads :o)</td>', 'congratulations on the blue ribbon! a first class entry indeed :o) all the best, ads :o)', '2007-03-14 07:54:34.000000', NULL, 0),
