(3465253, 480013, 74862, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by manniagni:</b></div><hr/><i> very nice composition. The contrast of red, blue and green is great - bit oversat?? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>x2 - great composition and perspective, but the red looks a bit blown</td>', 'Originally posted by manniagni: very nice composition. The contrast of red, blue and green is great - bit oversat??   x2 - great composition and perspective, but the red looks a bit blown', '2007-03-15 21:21:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3465254, 480525, 50695, '<td valign="top">good eye. fascinating combination of imagery.</td>', 'good eye. fascinating combination of imagery.', '2007-03-15 21:23:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3465258, 478139, 50695, '<td valign="top">cool picture. I get a real sense of exuberance. A motionless leap into wallness.</td>', 'cool picture. I get a real sense of exuberance. A motionless leap into wallness.', '2007-03-15 21:24:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3465281, 479172, 50695, '<td valign="top">I don''t see no speck or no hole. You crazy. <br/> <br/>This actually doesn''t look like a painting. It is in fact, kind of giving the finger to painting. And that''s a good thing.<br/> <br/>I call this, "Finger Painting." So let it be written, so let it be done.</td>', 'I don''t see no speck or no hole. You crazy.  This actually doesn''t look like a painting. It is in fact, kind of giving the finger to painting. And that''s a good thing. I call this, "Finger Painting." So let it be written, so let it be done.', '2007-03-15 21:32:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3465293, 479366, 50695, '<td valign="top">yes, showers clear your ass. that''s why we take showers. hahahaha I kill me. but seriously, folks, I love this photo. Great composition. Wonderful lines and textures. This picture has a terrific rhythm to it.</td>', 'yes, showers clear your ass. that''s why we take showers. hahahaha I kill me. but seriously, folks, I love this photo. Great composition. Wonderful lines and textures. This picture has a terrific rhythm to it.', '2007-03-15 21:35:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3465348, 479953, 50695, '<td valign="top"><b>Poetic Transference</b> <br/> <br/><i>for Philip Levine</i> <br/> <br/>Of all your old poet''s stories, <br/>the emperor who was a footstool, <br/>the pig who knows he will die, <br/>it is my own I keep giving to you, <br/>like a more obscure piece <br/>only the winking fanatics would know. <br/> <br/>Maybe I wanted your breath <br/>in the break of each line, or a folded, stapled <br/>cover I could close. <br/> <br/>Without even knowing <br/>what you look like, <br/>I cannot forget the day <br/>you recited it: <br/>the rain, the confetti and balloons in the gutter, <br/>how I almost drowned there in that lie. <br/> <br/><i>by Don Zirilli</i> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Poetic Transference  for Philip Levine  Of all your old poet''s stories, the emperor who was a footstool, the pig who knows he will die, it is my own I keep giving to you, like a more obscure piece only the winking fanatics would know.  Maybe I wanted your breath in the break of each line, or a folded, stapled cover I could close.  Without even knowing what you look like, I cannot forget the day you recited it: the rain, the confetti and balloons in the gutter, how I almost drowned there in that lie.  by Don Zirilli  ', '2007-03-15 21:53:36.000000', NULL, 0),
