(3786415, 480256, 5885, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by aKiwi:</b></div><hr/><i> You have to use better lighting for images like this.<br/>Don''t use the on camera flash.<br/>Experimenting with cheap Gloodlights from hardware stores can create astoundingly good pictures. Get the light to the side &amp; soften it by shooting through some sort of difuser.<br/>Beautiful model by the way. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree. Also, I think a vertical crop would have helped. This crop looks snapshotish. And I love redheads :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by aKiwi: You have to use better lighting for images like this.Don''t use the on camera flash.Experimenting with cheap Gloodlights from hardware stores can create astoundingly good pictures. Get the light to the side & soften it by shooting through some sort of difuser.Beautiful model by the way.   I agree. Also, I think a vertical crop would have helped. This crop looks snapshotish. And I love redheads :-)', '2007-06-14 23:41:58.000000', NULL, 0),
